From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:09:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] minimize: log window captures to the journal

A crash recorder has to tell whether a window capture was running when
the GPU faulted. Every capture, the hover preview's live session and the
one-shot thumbnails, now writes a `capture start` line (window app id,
buffer size, shm buffer format and the dmabuf device the compositor
offered), a `capture frame failed` line with the reason, and a
`capture end` line with the reason. A live session also logs
`capture resize` when the window size changes. Frame requests and ready
frames are debug lines, so the journal gets no per-frame noise.

Without RUST_LOG the default filter showed errors only, so no info line
of this applet reached the journal. It now shows this crate's info lines
and other crates' errors, on stderr, without colour codes unless stderr
is a terminal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BLrpLgiiwzH1vSG4u6dpEA

